.css-14on8x8{font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0em;line-height:1.6;font-weight:normal;color:var(--adaptiveGrey800);margin:24px 0 8px;}
Toss has earned ISO 22301 certification, the international standard for business continuity management, recognizing its ability to maintain critical services and recover quickly in the event of disruptions, disasters, or other business emergencies.
ISO 22301 is an internationally recognized standard for organizations that can effectively prepare for, respond to, and recover from operational disruptions while ensuring the continuity of critical business services. The certification is widely used by companies and public institutions to validate their business continuity capabilities against globally recognized standards.
To achieve the certification, Toss underwent a comprehensive assessment covering every stage of its business continuity management system, including business impact analysis, risk assessment, incident response and recovery planning, and operational reviews with business teams. The certification confirms that Toss's business continuity framework is not only well documented but also effectively implemented across the organization.
The certification reflects Toss' ongoing commitment to delivering reliable services to users. As the company operates a broad range of financial and consumer services, it has continued to strengthen its preparedness to minimize service disruptions and ensure operational resilience, even in unexpected situations.
Toss will continue to enhance its business continuity management system following the certification by regularly reviewing and refining its processes to keep pace with changes in its organization, systems, and operating environment. The company also plans to further strengthen its crisis response capabilities through continuous improvement and ongoing readiness.
"This certification confirms that we have established a robust framework to maintain critical services even during unexpected disruptions," a Toss representative said. "We will continue to strengthen our business continuity capabilities so users can rely on Toss with confidence, regardless of the circumstances."
